=2 Walkthrough
* Speak to {p:Sylvie} at {z:Western Adoulin} Waterfront (I-5) Waypoint #9 to begin the quest.
** {p:Geomancer} must be set as your main job to activate the quest. The quest can be done on any job.
* Speak to {n:Nhili Uvolep} at {z:Eastern Adoulin} (I-7), Sverdhried Hillock Waypoint #7, for a cutscene.
** If you still have the {p:Trial Wand} or get the WS trial wand from her, talk to her again until you get the correct cutscene with Sylvie, zoning is not necessary.
* Travel to (K-10) {z:Morimar Basalt Fields} Frontier Station and speak to {n:Vestavius}.
* Travel to (J-6) {z:Morimar Basalt Fields} (at the north-west corner of (J-6) which is accessible by traveling east from Bivouac #2) and examine the "Ergon Locus ???" (south of the giant rock, not sparkling) for a cutscene and to obtain {k:Silver luopan} Key Item.
** Those not in possession of the {k:Silver luopan} Key Item will receive a one-time {p:Bayld} reward; size of the reward depends on the number of players present for the defeat of the NM.
* Examine the Ergon Locus ??? a second time to spawn **{m:Deranged Ameretat}**.
** Has approximately 75k HP.
** The NM primarily uses Sweet Breath and Bad Breath. It is also capable of using Extremely Bad Breath (less than 50%HP), but the cast time is long enough to run out of range.
** The NM will not use Extremely Bad Breath as long as an enfeebling Indi- or Geo- effect is active.
** The NM has very high Magic Evasion and magic damage reduction and is immune to nearly all enfeebles including Stun.
** It is recommended to use ranged trusts; ie Apururu, Semih Lafihna, Tenzen II, Makki-Chebukki, etc.
* Upon defeating the {m:Deranged Ameretat}, examine the Ergon Locus ??? a third time for a cutscene.
** You will lose the {k:Silver luopan} Key Item.
* Return to {p:Sylvie} (I-5) {z:Western Adoulin} for the final cutscene and your rewards.
* You must wait a game day before beginning the next quest.

